{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"the-series-the-greedy-rule-and-finite-identities","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/the-series-the-greedy-rule-and-finite-identities","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=the-series-the-greedy-rule-and-finite-identities","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=the-series-the-greedy-rule-and-finite-identities","span":{"end_byte":135267,"end_line":1356,"start_byte":112658,"start_line":1103},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.thm-dynamics&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.thm-dynamics&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.thm-dynamics&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.thm-dynamics&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.thm-dynamics","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-dynamics"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-dynamics"],"id":"long.thm-dynamics","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 5.16 (Exact recurrences for the three branches)","locator":"Long record Theorem 5.16, p. 42, label thm:dynamics","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Fix $n\\ge5$. Among the quotient sums over subsets of $\\{2,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, let $D_n$ give the largest sum at most $T_n$ and let $B_n$ give the smallest sum strictly greater than $T_n$. Thus $D_n$ is the greedy support already defined. Put\n$$\nr=\\mathrm{rem}(n),\\qquad o=Q(B_n,2n)-T_n,\n$$\nand define the two correction terms by\n$$\np^- =\\sum_{d\\in D_n}\\bigl(2\\mathbf1_{d\\mid2n+1}\n                              +\\mathbf1_{d\\mid2n+2}\\bigr),\\qquad\n p^+ =\\sum_{d\\in B_n}\\bigl(2\\mathbf1_{d\\mid2n+1}\n                              +\\mathbf1_{d\\mid2n+2}\\bigr).\n$$\nBoth lie in $[0,2(n-2)]$, since $d\\ge2$ cannot divide both consecutive integers. The next remainder is\n$$\n\\mathrm{rem}(n+1)=\n \\begin{cases}\n 2^{n+1}-4o-p^+,&\\text{if }4o+p^+\\le2^{n+1}\\quad(\\mathrm U),\\\\\n 4r+2^{n+1}-p^-,&\\text{if not }\\mathrm U\\text{ and }\n                   4r+2^{n+1}-p^-<2^{n+2}+4\\quad(\\mathrm M),\\\\\n 4r-2^{n+1}-p^--4,&\\text{otherwise}\\quad(\\mathrm R).\n \\end{cases}\n$$\nConsequently, for $\\lambda_n=(\\mathrm{rem}(n)-2^n)/2^n$,\n$$\n\n \\lambda_{n+1}=\n \\begin{cases}\n -(4o+p^+)/2^{n+1},&\\mathrm U,\\\\\n 2\\lambda_n+2-p^-/2^{n+1},&\\mathrm M,\\\\\n 2\\lambda_n-(p^-+4)/2^{n+1},&\\mathrm R.\n \\end{cases}\n \\tag{III}\n$$*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-dynamics","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.thm-dynamics","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c170809